WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.780
Speaker 1: Another player is entering the 2024&nbsp;
Republican primary. It's former Arkansas Governor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:14.220
Asa Hutchinson who will be running against&nbsp;
Donald Trump, Nikki Haley and Vivek Ramaswamy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:22.560
He announced this when speaking to Jonathan Karl&nbsp;
from ABC. Not exactly making huge headlines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.340
understandably, but let's take a listen.
Speaker 5: When I spoke to you earlier this year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.940
you said you were thinking about running for&nbsp;
president. Have you made a decision? Are you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.920
running? I have made a decision. And my decision&nbsp;
is I'm going to run for president of the United&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:41.460
States. Wow. The formal announcement will be&nbsp;
later in April in Bentonville. I wanted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.660
make that'll be a real party player. That to&nbsp;
you, Jonathan. I am going to be running. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:51.720
the reason is I've traveled the country for six&nbsp;
months. I hear people talk about the leadership&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:57.180
of our country. And I'm convinced that people&nbsp;
want leaders that appeal to the best of America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.920
and not simply appeal to our worst instincts.
Speaker 1: I always find it funny when they say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.120
they've traveled the country, and I know it's sort&nbsp;
of like you have to do it and you have to say it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.260
but do you really need to travel the&nbsp;
country to figure out a lot of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.820
things? It's always a weird thing to hear.
Speaker 5: And that inspires me when I see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:20.760
everyday Americans. You're saying give us good&nbsp;
leadership, give us common sense, consistent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:27.540
conservatism and optimism about our great country.&nbsp;
And that inspires me. And I believe I can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.100
that kind of leader for the people of America.
Speaker 1: All right. So he has absolutely no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:37.320
shot, but it is interesting to see more people&nbsp;
enter. If I were a betting man and I'm not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:42.000
my guess is Asa Hutchinson doesn't even make&nbsp;
it past the first Republican primary. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.840
that being said, more candidates generally&nbsp;
does seem to be better for Donald Trump. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.980
more people there are running the Republican&nbsp;
primary, what we see in the polling is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:59.100
it helps Trump versus DeSantis. We have some&nbsp;
new ish polls. I'm trying to look at ones that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:04.860
are actually sort of like, well, well rated.&nbsp;
There's a Trafalgar Group poll, which is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:11.280
right leaning poll. It's a Multi-way poll. It&nbsp;
has Trump over DeSantis by 34 with Liz Cheney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:18.060
who doesn't seem to have any plan to run at 10%.&nbsp;
Then we have an insider advantage poll that's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:27.120
B rated poll. Trump over DeSantis by 33. And then&nbsp;
we have a B-plus rated YouGov poll. In this poll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.400
Trump does better with more candidates. This&nbsp;
isn't surprising. This is what we've seen when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:38.520
it is just Trump versus DeSantis. Trump leads&nbsp;
by 26 and when it is Trump versus a whole bunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:43.860
of. People. Trump leads by 31, and we could&nbsp;
go further, but this is sort of where we are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:51.420
right now. So interesting that Asa Hutchinson is&nbsp;
running. I truly wonder when people like this run.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.460
Are they sitting in a room where someone is&nbsp;
telling them you've got a shot at winning?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:02.100
Because they obviously don't? Or is it that&nbsp;
they're sitting in a room and advisers say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:07.620
you don't have a shot, but this might raise your&nbsp;
public profile, You might get yourself on a debate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:13.320
stage, and then you can parlay that into being a&nbsp;
contributor to Fox News or something like what is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:18.720
actually in their minds when they decide to run.&nbsp;
What do they think versus what is the reality of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.820
what can come from it and what is the basis on&nbsp;
which they're making these these decisions. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:31.080
an interesting thing. We now have a four way race&nbsp;
in the Republican primary with one of those four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.420
candidates under indictment. And we're going to&nbsp;
very closely follow the direction that this goes

